description: Planned exchange asset-recovery contract: on-chain trace to CEX freeze/recovery request boundaries.
alwaysApply: true
---

Canonical design: `solutions/exchange-asset-recovery.json` and `docs/security-integrations/exchange-asset-recovery.md`.
Keep status planned and executable false. Connect kill-chain on-chain reports to exchange stolen-funds desk / law-enforcement liaison / court / regulator channels without creating an executable exchange tool, API submission connector or credential.
Evidence packages pin tx refs to block height, API snapshot hash, fetch time and query window. Attribution levels are separate: on-chain provenance, third-party tracker label, exchange confirmation, court order return. Third-party labels are not on-chain proof; missing outflow is not proof of non-exit.
Live wallet status is observed at fetch time and re-verified before submission because hot wallets keep paying out. Freeze is not recovery; recovery is only finalized by a legal instrument.
Bind requests to exchange desk, purpose, immutable proposal/manifest digest, classification, wallet refs, amounts and expiry. Desk, purpose, manifest, wallet, channel, legal basis, authority expiry or material on-chain state change invalidate approval. Submission is not acknowledgment; freeze is not recovery; partial amounts are allowed.
Unknown, declined, expired and revoked states are preserved separately; never collapse an unknown outcome into submitted or safe. Reconcile submission and exchange ticket before retry. Revocation notifies the exchange and records the decision without claiming recall of submitted evidence.
Cross-border exchanges route through the international-investigation contract (MLAT/NCB); domestic channels do not submit abroad.
